title: what I am unsure of here
pid: 37d9cbe1-b3ba-41a5-8f9b-c78817b135e6
body: |2-
  - Whether the harm transfers. It was measured where episodes of a
    task were abstracted into lessons; our tending mostly moves notes.
    One test so far, of a tending that moved: it made no answer wrong
    ([[id:6e999046-a465-4003-a8aa-c0f223e77ec0][the probe test of Vic's tending of 2026-11-13]]). A tending that
    rewrites or raises a lesson is still untested.
  - Whether what tending moved behind a link is found again when it is
    needed. That depends on the link's words saying when to open it.
    In that test Sonnet named the link in half the answers it could no
    longer give, and Haiku almost never; the facts were safe only
    because the docs held most of them.
  - The cost figures are two days of one team.
  - The test costs about $7 a pair the first time, and some $2 to put
    the same probes to a later tending (measured once, on Vic's pair).
